From: fpvOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm: artosyn: BETAFPV VR04 HD Pro display

The Pro goggles drive their panel through a GM8773C: the SoC sends CEA
1080p60 on four 891 Mbps lanes, and the bridge, programmed over I2C (0x57),
sends the panel its init in low-power mode. Add the p1-goggle-pro-1080p
profile (stock's raster and lane rate from libpn_gm8773c.so of the P1 ground
firmware 2.1.4; the PLL divider scaled from the 928.8 Mbps one, the D-PHY
table left as it is) and a panel driver that replays stock's I2C sequence
once the video is up.

Written from the firmware alone; not run on a unit.

